       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the absolute ceiling)\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
